{
  "info": {
    "name": "Chat & Messages APIs",
    "description": "Test kit for the chat feature: direct/group/service/order-combined chats, membership, favourite/archive/block, leave with admin auto-promotion, messages (REST history/seen/delete; creation is SOCKET-ONLY, see docs/CHAT_SOCKET.md), and payment requests (REST create/accept/reject \u2014 '7. Payments' below).\n\nRULES:\n- A chat has a fixed set of members (chat_members) \u2014 REST never lets you act on a chat you're not a participant of.\n- Direct/order-combined chat creation is idempotent: calling it again with the same users/orderId returns the EXISTING chat instead of duplicating.\n- Message CREATION happens over Socket.IO's \"send message\" event, not REST \u2014 this collection only covers GET history / PUT seen / DELETE (per-user soft delete). Use docs/CHAT_SOCKET.md + a socket.io-client script to actually send messages for testing reply/media/payment/mention shapes.\n- Leaving a group as the admin auto-promotes the oldest remaining member \u2014 see '4. Membership & Leave'.\n- Payment requests/sends live under /api/payment, not /api/chat, and have NO chat/participant check \u2014 they only become visible in a chat once you separately emit 'send message' with the resulting paymentRequestId. Accepting/rejecting a request that IS attached to a chat message broadcasts 'message updated' into that chat (see docs/CHAT_SOCKET.md \u00a73) \u2014 see '7. Payments' below.\n\nORDER: 1) Run 'Login (user A)' and 'Login (user B)' \u2014 tokens auto-save. 2) Set otherUserId/secondUserId in Variables to real user ids on your DB. 3) Run 'Create direct chat' \u2014 chatId auto-saves. 4) Run any other request. For payment testing: 5) Run 'Create payment request' (as user A) \u2014 paymentRequestId auto-saves. 6) Emit 'send message' over the socket with { chatId, messageType: 'payment', paymentRequestId } to attach it to the chat (see docs/CHAT_SOCKET.md \u00a72). 7) Run 'Accept payment request' or 'Reject payment request' (as user B) to complete the flow.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://167.71.209.170:5001/api"
    },
    {
      "key": "token",
      "value": "eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.eyJ1c2VySWQiOjIsInRva2VuVmVyc2lvbiI6MywiaWF0IjoxNzg2MDYxNTU0fQ.7xPU8NP0QyNEHuDdtPKEQG54wkEh3ek8mS_ogqJf8C4"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "0. Auth",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Login (user A)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (json.token) { pm.collectionVariables.set('userToken', json.token); console.log('userToken saved'); }"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/login",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{userEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{userPassword}}\"\n}"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Login (user B)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (json.token) { pm.collectionVariables.set('secondUserToken', json.token); console.log('secondUserToken saved'); }",
                  "if (json.user && json.user.id) { pm.collectionVariables.set('otherUserId', json.user.id); }"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/login",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{secondUserEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{secondUserPassword}}\"\n}"
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "1. Chat Creation",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Create/reuse direct chat (userA <-> userB)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (json.data && json.data.id) { pm.collectionVariables.set('chatId', json.data.id); console.log('chatId saved:', json.data.id); }"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{userToken}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/chat/direct",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"userId\": {{otherUserId}}\n}"
            },
            "description": "Idempotent: calling again with the same pair of users returns the existing chat instead of creating a duplicate."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Create group chat",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (json.data && json.data.id) { pm.collectionVariables.set('groupChatId', json.data.id); console.log('groupChatId saved:', json.data.id); }"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{userToken}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/chat/group",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"groupName\": \"Design Team\",\n  \"groupImage\": \"https://cdn.example.com/groups/g1.png\",\n  \"memberIds\": [{{otherUserId}}],\n  \"lockSettings\": false\n}"
            },
            "description": "Caller becomes group_admin_id. memberIds should NOT include the caller \u2014 they're added automatically as admin."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Create service-request chat",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{userToken}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/chat/service",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"serviceId\": {{serviceId}},\n  \"teamId\": {{teamId}},\n  \"ownerId\": {{otherUserId}},\n  \"requestSubject\": \"Need a modern logo\",\n  \"requestDesc\": \"Looking for a minimalist logo in blue tones\"\n}"
            },
            "description": "Caller becomes customerId. ownerId is the service owner/team side of the conversation. Response includes a single-service 'service' object."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Create/reuse order-combined chat",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{userToken}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/chat/order",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"orderId\": {{orderId}},\n  \"ownerId\": {{otherUserId}},\n  \"services\": [\n    { \"serviceId\": 77, \"teamId\": 3, \"status\": 1 },\n    { \"serviceId\": 81, \"teamId\": 3, \"status\": 1 },\n    { \"serviceId\": 84, \"teamId\": 8, \"status\": 1 }\n  ]\n}"
            },
            "description": "Idempotent by orderId, NOT by service list \u2014 calling again with the same orderId returns the existing chat even if you pass different services. Response's 'service' object includes service_order_id + service_ids[]."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "2. Read",
      "item": [
